The center of a group G consists of all those elements x in G such that xg = gx for all g in G. This is a normal subgroup of G.
The similarly named notion for a semigroup is defined likewise and it is a subsemigroup.","description":"Index of articles associated with the same name","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}
